\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Corollary}
\title{Grading and index under lifted symmetries}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{A lift whose image has determinant one preserves the two
eigenspaces of the chosen #{\Gamma} on #{S}. A lift of determinant
minus one interchanges them. The same rule holds for a second
self-adjoint involution #{\Gamma'} anticommuting with every
#{\varepsilon_j} if it commutes with #{\Gamma}.}

\p{Let #{G} be a subgroup of the lift over determinant one
and let it act on a finite-dimensional #{k}-space #{V} with a
grading #{\Gamma_V}, where #{k} is a field in which #{2} and
#{|G|} are invertible. Suppose the action commutes with
#{\Gamma_V} and with a #{k}-linear endomorphism #{A} satisfying
#{\Gamma_V A=-A\Gamma_V}. For each irreducible #{G}-type the
multiplicity difference between the positive and negative parts
of #{\ker A^{\dim V}} equals the same difference for #{V}.
On #{S} the even lifts already commute with the chosen grading.
Commutation with the operator #{A} is an additional hypothesis.}

\proof{
\p{The involution #{\Gamma} anticommutes with each
#{f_j=\Gamma\varepsilon_j} and commutes with every
#{u_{jk}}, whose nonconstant term contains two direction
operators. Moving it through a word gives the determinant sign
of \ref{fdip-016R}, also for inverses. This proves preservation
or exchange of its eigenspaces. For #{\Gamma'} the same computation
with #{f_j} uses #{\Gamma'\Gamma=\Gamma\Gamma'}.
Indeed, since #{\varepsilon_j} is invertible and anticommutes
with #{\Gamma'}, anticommutation with #{f_j} is equivalent to
that commutation with #{\Gamma}.}

\p{Put #{d=\dim V}. The stable splitting in \ref{fdip-016K}
at order two gives #{V=\ker A^d\oplus\im A^d}. Both parts are
#{G}-stable, since #{G} commutes with #{A}, and grading-stable.
On the image #{A} bijects the positive and negative spaces
equivariantly. Their multiplicities therefore agree. Averaging
a projection over #{G} gives invariant complements as in
\ref{fdip-016F}, so multiplicities add under the direct sum.
Subtracting cancels the image contributions. This is the
irreducible-type index of \ref{fdip-013S} for the supplied
action on #{V}.}
}
